# Backend Proxy Rule

This project runs inside a Qt WebEngine environment where the frontend has NO direct external network access. All HTTP requests to external URLs must go through the backend proxy.

## Endpoints

- **Images**: `POST /api/v1/proxy/image` — use `proxyImageUrl()` from `@renderer/utils/proxyImage` or the `useProxiedImage` hook
- **General HTTP**: `POST /api/v1/network/fetch` — for arbitrary GET/POST to external services
- **Search**: `POST /api/v1/network/search` — for search engine queries

## Rules

1. NEVER use `fetch()`, `XMLHttpRequest`, or `<img src="https://...">` to access external URLs directly
2. For external images, use `proxyImageUrl()` or `useProxiedImage` hook — they handle 3-layer caching (memory, IndexedDB, backend disk)
3. For non-image HTTP requests, use the `/api/v1/network/fetch` backend endpoint
4. Localhost URLs (`127.0.0.1`, `localhost`) are exempt — they reach the local backend server
5. `data:` and `blob:` URLs are exempt — they are already local

## Detecting External URLs

Use `isExternalUrl()` from `@renderer/utils/proxyImage` to check if a URL needs proxying.
